eparation, and sale of thermal coal, sold primarily to electric utilities; surface mining extraction processes, coal with a lower sulfur content, and Btu; and mining sub-bituminous coal deposits. It also supplies coal primarily to electricity generators, industrial facilities, and steel manufacturers. The company was founded in 1883 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James C. Grech | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $715K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Peabody Energy Corporation is a mid-cap energy business with a $2.1B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $78M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): durably derated by the market; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in BTU Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link